Looking at the comment: each bit is cleared if the corresponding bit in `set` was set, and unchanged otherwise.

<code>assert \forall int i; i>=0; (\old(set.get(i)) => !this.get(i)) && (!\old(set.get(i)) => this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment, I need to express: for every bit index, if the corresponding bit in `set` was set, this bit is cleared (false); otherwise it's left unchanged.

The relevant observer is `get(int bitIndex)`. Since `set` is not modified, I use `set.get(i)` directly, and `\old(this.get(i))` for the prior value.

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i; (set.get(i) => !this.get(i)) && (!set.get(i) => this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
